frontend/src/commands/factories/README.md:1:# Operation Sequence Factories
frontend/src/commands/factories/README.md:5:Operation Sequence Factories encapsulate common multi-operation patterns used across tools and command builders. They promote testability, reusability, and maintainability by centralizing complex sequencing logic.
frontend/src/commands/factories/README.md:12:- `GuideSequenceFactory` - Handles guide creation with conditional sibling
frontend/src/commands/factories/README.md:13:- `IntersectionSequenceFactory` - Dispatches to correct intersection type and handles siblings
frontend/src/commands/factories/README.md:14:- `DeletionSequenceFactory` - Handles cascade deletion with topological sorting
frontend/src/commands/factories/README.md:18:- `GenericSequenceFactory` - Abstract pattern requiring caller to know internals
frontend/src/commands/factories/README.md:46:  // Operations execute immediately
frontend/src/commands/factories/README.md:56:- Operations execute immediately (world state updated for subsequent ops)
